    "body": "Fixes #42097.\n\n**Problem:** an `--embed` server whose UI went away (e.g. its TUI process was killed / the terminal window closed) never exits if an error message is emitted while it is exiting. `getout()` calls `wait_return()` when `did_emsg` is set, and `wait_return()` only skips the hit-enter prompt in headless mode (5b34c2a). A server that had a UI and lost it is not headless, so it blocks forever waiting for `<Enter>` and is left behind as an orphan (PPID 1), together with its children (`:terminal` jobs etc.). In practice a corrupt ShaDa file is enough to trigger it on every exit; I had 100+ such orphans accumulate.\n\n**Solution:** also skip the prompt when exiting with no UI attached (`!ui_active() && (headless_mode || exiting)`).\n\nI kept this limited to exiting, so a server that is temporarily without a UI (e.g. after `:detach`) keeps its current hit-enter behaviour; happy to widen it to plain `!ui_active()` if that is preferred.\n\n**Test:** `API nvim_get_mode exits after UI detached even if an error occurs during exit` starts a non-headless server, attaches and detaches a UI, points `shadafile` at an unparseable file and runs `:qall!`. Before: the server never exits (the test fails after 2s). After: it exits. Related `vim_spec` tests (`prompt`, `nvim_get_mode`, `nvim_command_output`) and `ui/messages_spec.lua` pass; `make lintc` and `stylua --check` are clean.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01NnWcWgDdRRffTx4vvYxfUX\n",
